{
  "id": "Compound::DB01129 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Rabeprazole exhibits a strong binding interaction with Cyp2c9, a cytochrome P450 enzyme, which is implicated in the metabolism of various substrates. This binding is consistent across multiple paths, with all three evidence streams showing Rabeprazole interacting with Cyp2c9 and subsequently participating in the activity of limonene monooxygenase, a key enzyme in the oxidation of limonene. The shared involvement of Cyp2c9 in the oxidation of limonene, whether through (s)-limonene 6- or 7-monooxygenase activity, suggests a common functional pathway. The integration of these pathways implies that Rabeprazole may modulate Cyp2c19 through the regulation of Cyp2c9 activity, potentially affecting the metabolism of substrates that are oxidized by Cyp2c19. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Rabeprazole and Cyp2c19, where the inhibition of Cyp2c9 activity could influence the activity of Cyp2c19, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
